r conditions; or ask for Visitor Safety at 780-852-6155.\u003c/em\u003e\u003c/strong\u003e\u003c/p\u003e","confidence":{"rating":{"value":"high","display":"High"}},"summaries":[{"type":{"value":"avalanche-summary","display":"Avalanche Summary"},"content":" \u003cp\u003eDanger is highest after new snowfall, rain, or wind transport.\u0026nbsp;\u0026nbsp; Early season faceting may have weakened the bond of the thin fall snowpack to steep ice gullies/faces.\u0026nbsp; Use extra caution in high, icy arenas – Persistent Slabs have surprised parties in recent years, e.g. late season Mt Athabasca climbers.\u0026nbsp; Avalanche season is here: do your own avalanche forecasting; carry a transceiver, shovel and probe; and to know how to use them.\u003c/p\u003e"},{"type":{"value":"snowpack-summary","display":"Snowpack Summary"},"content":" \u003cp\u003e\u003ca target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://avalanche.ca/early-season-conditions\"\u003eAn early season overview\u003c/a\u003e\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eWatch out for alpine areas as they gain enough snow for avalanches over the next couple of weeks. High bowls, gullies, and around ridgelines are classic spots for early season avalanches.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eVast numbers of open late summer crevasses are now deceptively hidden, by very thin bridges of wind-blown new snow.\u0026nbsp; Roping up and diligent probing, and glacier reading experience are all critical for safe glacier travel.\u003c/p\u003e"},{"type":{"value":"weather-summary","display":"Weather Summary"},"content":" \u003cp\u003eFor current weather conditions, see the\u0026nbsp;\u003ca target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.avalanche.ca/map\"\u003etelemetry stations\u0026nbsp;\u003c/a\u003eon the Avalanche Canada map page.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u0026nbsp;\u003ca target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer nofollow\" href=\"https://www.avalanche.ca/weather/forecast\"\u003eMountain Weather Forecast\u003c/a\u003e is available from Avalanche Canada\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003eDetailed local forecasts are available on your favorite weather app.\u003c/p\u003e\u003cp\u003e\u003cbr\u003e\u003c/p\u003e"}],"dangerRatings":[{"date":{"value":"2026-11-13T21:00:00Z","display":"Friday"},"ratings":{"alp":{"display":"Alpine","rating":{"value":"earlyseason","display":"Early Season"}},"tln":{"display":"Treeline","rating":{"value":"earlyseason","display":"Early Season"}},"btl":{"display":"Below Treeline","rating":{"value":"norating","display":"No Rating"}}}},{"date":{"value":"2026-11-14T21:00:00Z","display":"Saturday"},"ratings":{"alp":{"display":"Alpine","rating":{"value":"earlyseason","display":"Early Season"}},"tln":{"display":"Treeline","rating":{"value":"earlyseason","display":"Early Season"}},"btl":{"display":"Below Treeline","rating":{"value":"norating","display":"No Rating"}}}},{"date":{"value":"2026-11-15T21:00:00Z","display":"Sunday"},"ratings":{"alp":{"display":"Alpine","rating":{"value":"earlyseason","display":"Early Season"}},"tln":{"display":"Treeline","rating":{"value":"earlyseason","display":"Early Season"}},"btl":{"display":"Below Treeline","rating":{"value":"norating","display":"No Rating"}}}}],"problems":[],"terrainAndTravelAdvice":[],"message":null,"season":null,"comment":null,"isFullTranslation":true},"version":1,"owner":{"value":"parks-jasper","display":"Parks Canada","isExternal":false,"url":"Parks Canada"},"notifications":[{"type":"info","content":"Seasonal closures for caribou conservation in Jasper National Park are in effect from November to May. For more information, \u003ca href=\"https://www.pc.gc.ca/en/pn-np/ab/jasper/nature/conservation/retablissement-caribou-recovery/mesuresap-bcactions\"\u003eclick here.\u003c/a\u003e"}],"media":{"images":[]}},{"id":"cf50334f-3c6b-478b-b02f-dd9ecb233074_010016cb778a7962e0174e68d5a278372db93924e19e450052de07b95eb72c85","slug":"cf50334f-3c6b-478b-b02f-dd9ecb233074_010016cb778a7962e0174e68d5a278372db93924e19e4